::meta{crate: tomet-edit, dependencies: list(motem-syntax, tomet-address, tomet-ast, tomet-config, tomet-cst, tomet-parser, tomet-tree, tomet-validator, tomet-vault), dependents: list(tomet, tomet-tests)}

=[tomet-edit]

==[tomet-edit]

Backend-neutral editable tree model of a Tomet document for collaborative editing.

==[Architecture & Core Principles]

- ("CRDT-Agnostic Model") This crate provides an in-memory, tree-structured document model with opaque [`NodeId`]s,
designed to bridge to external collaborative runtimes (such as Loro, Yjs, or Automerge).
It depends on zero CRDT libraries, networking, or session transport code.
- ("CST Foundation & Guaranteed Invariant") The model is derived from the Concrete Syntax Tree (`tomet-cst`). Trivia (whitespace,
newlines, comments) is preserved alongside nodes.
Guaranteed Invariant: Importing and immediately exporting without edits is 100% byte-identical
to the original input source across the entire corpus (`export_doc(&import_source(src)) == src`).
- ("Text as Raw String (Paragraphs & Headings)") Prose within paragraphs, headings, and element content is held as raw text rather than
inline marks. Structure in the model is retained where identity, moving, and keys matter
(sections, blocks, attributes), allowing CRDTs to merge text via character-level sequences
without fragile structured-mark nesting.
- ("First-Class Move & Closed Edit Operations") [`EditOp`] provides a minimal, closed set of operations (`Insert`, `Delete`, `Move`, `EditText`, `SetAttribute`).
`Move` is a first-class operation, directly supported by tree-based CRDTs (e.g. Loro's MovableTree).
[`EditOp::SetAttribute`] allows key-level manipulation of an element's `{}` data, `()` args, and `#()` id slot.
- ("Post-Edit Diagnostics") Collaborative engines merge writes without rejecting them. [`diagnose_doc`] exports the edited
document to source text and re-parses it with the full validator to report duplicate IDs,
schema errors, or broken syntax after concurrent merges. [`diagnose_doc_in`] does it as a
document of a vault: its vocabularies, the types its settings declare, its blueprint.

==[Module address]

Address-based resolution and editing operations for [`EditDoc`].

Provides resolution of address strings (such as `#intro`, `#item(0)`,
`#intro.item(1)`, `#meta.icon`, etc.) to [`NodeId`]s, attribute values,
or text content, along with high-level mutation helpers.

===[Structs]

====[struct AddressPath]

A parsed intra-document address path.

===[Enums]

====[enum BaseTarget]

The base/root anchor target of an address path.

====[enum Step]

A traversal step along an address path.

===[Functions]

====[fn parse_address_path]

Parses a Tomet address string into an [`AddressPath`].

==[Module diagnostics]

Post-edit diagnostics over an [`EditDoc`].

A collaborative editing runtime (e.g. CRDT) merges concurrent edits without
rejecting writes. After applying edits, this module exports the document back
to source text, parses it with the AST parser (`parse_document`), and runs
`validate_document` to report duplicate IDs or validation warnings.

===[Enums]

====[enum PostEditReport]

The diagnostic report of an edited document.

===[Functions]

====[fn diagnose_doc]

Diagnoses an [`EditDoc`] by exporting to source, parsing with [`parse_document`],
and running [`validate_document`].

That knows `std` alone, as a document in a vault with no settings and no
vocabularies would; [`diagnose_doc_in`] is the report for a document in a vault.

====[fn diagnose_doc_in]

Diagnoses an [`EditDoc`] as a document of `vault`: what `tomet check`
finds without the disk ([`Vault::diagnostics`]) -- the vocabularies the
document has in scope, the types the vault's settings declare for `::meta`
fields, and the blueprint of `blueprints` that its `::kind` names.

==[Module doc]

The root `EditDoc` managing tree nodes and IDs.

===[Structs]

====[struct EditDoc]

An editable tree model of a Tomet document.

==[Module export]

Serializes an [`EditDoc`] back into Tomet source text.

===[Functions]

====[fn export_doc]

Exports an [`EditDoc`] back to a Tomet source string.

Guaranteed Invariant: An import followed by export with no edits is byte-identical
to the input source:
`export(&import_source(src)) == src`

==[Module import]

Imports a concrete syntax tree (CST) into an [`EditDoc`].

===[Functions]

====[fn import_source]

Parses `src` into a CST and imports it into an [`EditDoc`].

====[fn import_cst]

Imports an existing Rowan CST [`SyntaxNode`] into an [`EditDoc`].

==[Module node]

Node and child definitions for `tomet-edit`.

===[Structs]

====[struct NodeId]

An opaque, unique identifier for a node in an [`EditDoc`].

====[struct Node]

An editable node in a Tomet document tree.

===[Enums]

====[enum ChildItem]

An entry in a child list: either layout trivia (whitespace/comment) or a child node.

====[enum AttrGroup]

Target attribute slot or group on an element.

====[enum NodeKind]

Specific variant of an editable node.

==[Module op]

===[Enums]

====[enum EditError]

====[enum EditOp]

A closed set of atomic edit operations on an [`EditDoc`].
